 "text": "Hello, how are things going? Definitely. Many people here speak English, but knowing a few basic phrases in Thai will make ordering food and finding your way easier. Fair enough. If you do decide to learn, the basic verb tenses are easy. The driver will tell you which bag is first. Yes, they will. Then the next bag goes in, and so on. Yes, bags can be Swaped out. The driver will tell you which bag is first. Then the next bag goes in, and so on. The toughest one is probably the steep descent. Push with your legs, keep your brakes on and take them off just enough to keep the bike under you.",
